Help For The Decoders

Decoders: c opens CW decoding; r opens RTTY decoding. Capture starts on entry when setup allows it. Only one decoder runs at a time.
Inside a decoder: e explicitly stops or restarts capture. q says Back and leaves capture running. q again returns to the main controls. Returning to another decoder stops the previous capture. YAC exit stops capture and restores native decoder settings.
v reviews the latest text; comma reviews earlier text; full stop later text. Review chunks are 60 characters. n clears received text. New text appears automatically only inside the decoder view; capture continues quietly elsewhere. Terminal speech and braille read that text using your existing accessibility setup. h gives this help.
TS-590SG CW: select CW mode first. Native decoder tracks speed automatically. Plus and minus adjust its threshold, 1 to 30. YAC preserves decoder enable and Auto Information settings and restores them on stop.
Other supported radios: CW uses received audio, not CAT text. This first version is experimental and uses a fixed pitch with automatic timing. Install the optional requirements-decoders.txt dependencies and explicitly configure cw_audio_device in yac.ini. Match cw_audio_pitch_hz to the received tone and choose cw_audio_channel for Main/Sub. No microphone or default device is selected automatically. Decoder pauses when transmit status is detected or cannot be read; polling is not instantaneous. Audio distortion, noise and hand sending can cause mistakes.
IC-705 RTTY: select RTTY mode first. YAC uses the uniquely identified companion USB port B, preserving its function. It refuses DV/Weather use or port-B SEND/keying assignments. If identification is ambiguous, set rtty_port to the verified companion port; it must belong to this radio. Other RTTY models currently report Not supported.
A start failure can mean wrong mode, missing audio dependency, invalid audio input, ambiguous USB ports, keying assignments or rejected CAT settings. Details go to the YAC debug log. No decoder transmits or changes operating frequency, mode or power.

d then a: guided receive audio setup; h inside explains selection and level checks.

Decoder could not start. Check mode and decoder setup; press h for help.
Decoder input lost; capture stopped. Check radio settings.

